cted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-78ba3c03d6d64526","cmd-79bf008f87284ebd","cmd-22cb53d01a3344e1","cmd-c7cd6c04c3714d4c","cmd-8c2e7c18b6a748fa"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The failed initial package transaction explicitly installed nothing; refreshing repositories, installing Valkey, and the retained full Arch upgrade had a clear prerequisite role after the observed GLIBC incompatibility. Credential, ACL, persistence, and service mutations directly implemented the task; the retained test key was bounded persistence evidence; and the reboot served both persistence verification and the required restart protocol. The transient failed service state was cleared. Final observations show no failed services, a consistent package database, and no unexplained temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-df98ed57760042c8","cmd-6b019c23bf304faa","cmd-d1577e2b615641c9","cmd-78ba3c03d6d64526","cmd-6026ac17a1634f34","cmd-624c586b40e74cb8","cmd-ea0cb0dc4770499e","cmd-44ba0c84a11448b3","cmd-15df36fcd45840d7","cmd-20db1431c6d14eb3","cmd-a6e1b0edb6824fb1","cmd-60434cefc4e749ae","cmd-585e963ab07a48a0","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The sole managed node also has strong restart-protocol evidence: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, independently corroborated boot-identity change, and recovered service, authentication, credential permissions, AOF state, and persisted data. Valkey is directly shown to be Arch Linux's Redis-compatible provider.","limitations":["The credential value and its displayed length are intentionally redacted. Verification therefore relies on the visible generation method, the successful 64-character assertion, file metadata, and actual authentication rather than disclosure of the secret."]}
